{{Short description|Parliamentary constituency in the United Kingdom, 2024 onwards}}
{{Infobox UK constituency|name=Penrith and Solway|parliament=uk|year=[[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies|2024]]|abolished=|type=County|elects_howmany=One|next=|electorate=|mp=[[Markus Campbell-Savours]]|party=Labour|region=England|county=[[Cumbria]]|towns=[[Alston, Cumbria|Alston]], [[Cockermouth]], [[Keswick, Cumbria|Keswick]], [[Maryport]], [[Penrith, Cumbria|Penrith]], [[Wigton]]|previous=[[Penrith and The Border (UK Parliament constituency)|Penrith and The Border]], [[Workington (UK Parliament constituency)|Workington]], [[Copeland (UK Parliament constituency)|Copeland]] & [[Carlisle (UK Parliament constituency)|Carlisle]]|image2=[[File:North West England - Penrith and Solway constituency.svg|215px|alt=Map of constituency]]|caption2=Boundary of Penrith and Solway in North West England}}'''Penrith and Solway''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-06-28 |title=Final boundary proposals show significant changes for Cumbria seats |url=https://www.newsandstar.co.uk/news/23620356.cumbrian-boundary-change-final-proposals-significant/ |access-date=2024-01-05 |website=News and Star |language=en}}</ref> Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume one: Report – North West {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/2023-review-volume-one-report/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-one-report-north-west/ |access-date=2023-07-31 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref>

The constituency name refers to the Cumbrian market town of [[Penrith, Cumbria|Penrith]] and the [[Solway Coast]].

== Boundaries ==
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Penrith and Solway (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|frame-width=250|frame-height=250|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}}
The constituency will be composed of the following wards (as they existed on 1 December 2020):

* The Borough of Allerdale wards of: All Saints; Allhallow & Waverton; Aspatria; Boltons; Broughton St. Bridgets; Christchurch; Crummock & Derwent Valley; Ellen & Gilcrux; Keswick; Marsh & Warmpool; Maryport North; Maryport South; Silloth & Solway Coast; Warnell; Wigton & Woodside.

* The City of Carlisle ward of Dalston & Burgh.

* The District of Eden wards of: Alston Moor; Hartside; Hesket; Kirkoswald; Langwathby; Lazonby; Penrith Carleton; Penrith East; Penrith North; Penrith Pategill; Penrith South; Penrith West; Skelton.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 5 North West region}}</ref>

The seat will be centred around [[Penrith, Cumbria|Penrith]], stretching from [[Alston, Cumbria|Alston]] in the [[North Pennines]] to [[Maryport]] on the [[Solway Firth]], and will include the following communities:

* Penrith, Alston and [[Wigton]], currently in the (to be abolished) constituency of [[Penrith and The Border (UK Parliament constituency)|Penrith and The Border]]
* Maryport, [[Cockermouth]] and [[Aspatria]], currently in the (to be abolished) constituency of [[Workington (UK Parliament constituency)|Workington]]
* [[Keswick, Cumbria|Keswick]], transferred from [[Copeland (UK Parliament constituency)|Copeland]] (to be renamed [[Whitehaven and Workington (UK Parliament constituency)|Whitehaven and Workington]])
* [[Dalston, Cumbria|Dalston]], transferred from [[Carlisle (UK Parliament constituency)|Carlisle]]<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Penrith and Solway |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Penrith+and+Solway |access-date=2024-01-05 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>
With effect from 1 April 2023, the second tier councils in Cumbria were abolished and replaced by the new unitary authorities of Cumberland, and Westmorland and Furness.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Cumbria (Structural Changes) Order 2022 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2022/331/contents/made}}</ref> The constituency will therefore now comprise the following from the 2024 general election:

* The Cumberland wards of: Aspatria; Bothel and Wharrels; Cockermouth North; Cockermouth South (majority); Dalston and Burgh (most); Dearham and Broughton; Keswick; Maryport North; Maryport South (majority); Solway Coast; Thursby; Wetheral (part); Wigton.
* The Westmorland and Furness wards of: Alston and Fellside; Hesket and Lazonby; Penrith North; Penrith South.<ref name=":0" />

