== Elections ==
This area has elected [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] candidates to be MP since its creation in 1983, with majorities of more than 15%; therefore, until 2019, it could have been seen as a [[safe seat]]. Unlike the other two Bolton seats, it has remained safely Labour. This is also reflected by the majority of wards returning councillors for Labour; a notably stronger ward for the [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative Party]] to date has been Hulton, which has often returned Conservative councillors.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.bolton.gov.uk/website/Pages/Electionsnoticesandresults.aspx|title=Bolton MB Council Election Results|access-date=24 December 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120923224051/http://www.bolton.gov.uk/website/pages/Electionsnoticesandresults.aspx|archive-date=23 September 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref>

