'''Wyre and Preston North''' was a [[county constituency]] represented in the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] of the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom]]. Created in 2010, it elected one [[Member of Parliament (United Kingdom)|Member of Parliament]] (MP) by the [[first past the post]] voting system.

It was formed from parts of the [[Ribble Valley (UK Parliament constituency)|Ribble Valley]], [[Fylde (UK Parliament constituency)|Fylde]], and [[Lancaster and Wyre (UK Parliament constituency)|Lancaster and Wyre]] constituencies.

Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], the seat was abolished. Subject to moderate boundary changes, with its area being split between five other constituencies, to be first contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume one: Report – North West {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/2023-review-volume-one-report/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-one-report-north-west/ |access-date=2023-07-21 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref><ref name=":19">{{Cite news |date=2023-06-28 |title=Defence Secretary Ben Wallace to lose seat in Commons boundary changes |language=en-GB |work=BBC News |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-politics-66045931 |access-date=2023-07-05}}</ref>

The seat's only MP was [[Ben Wallace (politician)|Ben Wallace]] of the [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative Party]], former [[Secretary of State for Defence]]. He announced in 2023 that he would not seek re-election at the 2024 general election.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2023-07-15 |title=Ben Wallace to quit as defence secretary at next cabinet reshuffle |language=en-GB |work=BBC News |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-66213245 |access-date=2023-07-21}}</ref>

==Boundaries==	
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Wyre and Preston North (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|text=Map of boundaries 2010-2024}}
Wyre and Preston North was created as the sixteenth seat of the county of [[Lancashire]] by the [[Boundary Commission for England]] prior to the [[2010 United Kingdom general election|2010 general election]]. It contained the Fulwood and rural areas of [[City of Preston, Lancashire|Preston]] and many small towns and villages of [[Borough of Wyre|Wyre]].

The seat contained the Wyre towns of [[Poulton-le-Fylde]], [[Garstang]], [[St Michael's On Wyre]], [[Catterall]] and parts of [[Thornton, Lancashire|Thornton]]. From Preston are added the suburban Fulwood area and the rural parishes such as Woodplumpton, Barton, Broughton, Goosnargh and Grimsargh. The electoral wards used in the creation are:

*From Preston: [[Cadley, Lancashire|Cadley]], College, Garrison, [[Greyfriars, Preston|Greyfriars]], [[Preston Rural East]], [[Preston Rural North]], [[Sharoe Green]]
*From Wyre: Breck, Brock, Cabus, Calder, [[Carleton, Lancashire|Carleton]], Catterall, [[Garstang]], [[Great Eccleston]], Hambleton and Stalmine-with-Staynall, Hardhorn, High Cross, Norcross, Staina, Tithebarn.

=== Abolition ===
Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], the seat was abolished prior to the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]], with parts distributed between five neighbouring constituencies:<ref name=":0" />

* [[Garstang]] and surrounding rural areas to [[Lancaster and Fleetwood (UK Parliament constituency)|Lancaster and Fleetwood]] (to be renamed [[Lancaster and Wyre (UK Parliament constituency)|Lancaster and Wyre]])
* The area comprising parts of the community of [[Thornton, Lancashire|Thornton]] to [[Blackpool North and Cleveleys (UK Parliament constituency)|Blackpool North and Cleveleys]] (to be renamed [[Blackpool North and Fleetwood (UK Parliament constituency)|Blackpool North and Fleetwood]])
* [[Poulton-le-Fylde]] to the constituency of [[Fylde (UK Parliament constituency)|Fylde]]
* Rural areas to the north of [[Preston, Lancashire|Preston]] and central areas of [[Fulwood, Lancashire|Fulwood]] to [[Ribble Valley (UK Parliament constituency)|Ribble Valley]]
* Outer areas of Fulwood to [[Preston (UK Parliament constituency)|Preston]]

